<title>UK: Bradford &amp; Bingley B/S sets 125 million stg bond.</title>
<headline>Bradford &amp; Bingley B/S sets 125 million stg bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following subordinated callable bond was announced by joints HSBC Markets and SBC Warburg.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BRADFORD AND BINGLEY BUILDING SOCIETY</p>
<p> AMT    125 MLN STG   COUPON     **	  MATURITY   *27.DEC.11</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  **	  PAY DATE    07.NOV.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.50	REOFFER    **	  SPREAD	+85 BP</p>
<p> NOTES    **TO BE PRICED LATER.</p>
<p>	     *CALL AT PAR AFTER 10 YEARS. IF NOT CALLED COUPON</p>
<p>		WILL BE RESET IF NECESSARY TO YIELD 185 BP OVER.</p>
<p> MOODY	=	   LISTING    LONDON    PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  =	   DENOMS (K) 100	 SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  BRITAIN   TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 7.50 PCT GILT DUE 2006</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
